# Activate a pinned governance workflow after review

The template does not enable a workflow by default. First seed the copied bundle
in a reviewed PR with this caller inactive. After that consumer baseline is merged,
add this caller in a separate activation PR using the human-approved backbone
workflow commit SHA instead of `PIN_APPROVED_COMMIT`. Confirm private-repository workflow access
with the owner first. A valid-looking SHA alone is not proof of approval or access.

```yaml
name: Engineering Backbone
on:
  pull_request:
  push:
    branches: [{{ base_branch | tojson }}]
permissions:
  contents: read
jobs:
  governance:
    uses: Artifaktory/engineering-backbone/.github/workflows/governance-checks.yml@PIN_APPROVED_COMMIT
    permissions:
      contents: read
```

Supplying `backbone_workflow_ref` during installation emits an active caller;
do that only when a complete reviewed bundle already exists on the consumer base.
Otherwise the first adoption PR fails closed. Existing
`.github/workflows/engineering-backbone.yml` is preserved. There are no secrets or
private source checkout tokens: the workflow runs the consumer base's validator,
schemas and dependency lock against the candidate with `--trusted-base`.
It never executes the candidate validator or installs its dependencies.
Keep language-specific checks in the consuming project's existing CI.

`backbone_workflow_ref` is installation-only. Changing activation or an existing
pin needs a separate reviewed workflow migration. A manually owned caller can be
added or repinned without editing installation-only saved answers; an ordinary
Copier baseline update rejects changing that selection.

PR checks compare explicit base/head revisions. Push checks compare the previous
push commit to the current commit; a zero previous SHA cannot supply trusted
consumer tooling. Manual dispatch validates the selected candidate using the
repository default branch's trusted bundle; an unmerged selected commit cannot
supply its own trusted tooling. Whitespace is checked against the selected
commit's parent (or the empty tree for a root commit), while policy is compared
against the default branch. Source mode is reserved for the backbone
repository. Keep the caller and its immutable pin under protected human review.
